editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **The Last Bout** (~4,500–5,000): Rooke chalks it in the dark; the bluff and the town come; the Crown yard counted one last time; Ephram takes the sunward mark; the threes and the short beat; **the band refused — the lid comes off** [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: the Norhold rates and past them, shown on the bluff for the first time; audit A3] ("There it is. Three years. Again." [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "Two years"; Cael has been on the bluff since B4's start, so nearly three years; or no count; audit B7]); no flag; the reach in earnest, its price written the night before; the commitment engine turned; two touches to one [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "two flags to one"; the Crown-yard format is stated once, as two touches or as Rooke's own trial rule (OWNER #39); audit B2]; **the Blade notice**; Rooke's "Both. Enter both."; Gault's nod; Withrow last out; Lira's sentence; the boards ritual and **"Still glad."**; not told — the covenant's cost entered; the first pull (a lintel's edge); Anchor left in the kit and why; the empty yard: **"Good room."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- Brom never signs, refuses nothing in writing, and does not open the envelope.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:215:"The third is certification." For the first time he looked at Karis, only at Karis, and Cael understood that the not looking at himself was being chosen, and chosen again, every moment. "Before this year is out the seat will send to my desk for my certificate on the protocol for a re-evaluation at Halcenvane. I have known it was coming since the convening. I meant to sign it, because the protocol is sound, and in forty years I have never refused my name to a sound protocol." He lifted his hand off the table. "When it comes, I shall decline. It is the only sentence I have left that they still need."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:- **The escort order**: the lodge's posted board; Withrow requires it read aloud (eighty-one words); Bracken's minute forty on a seal he cannot place; the refusal; "voluntarily" aimed at an empty gallery; no written refusal demanded; the refectory by noon; **Rooke eats in the open seat**; Gault: "I have written that down."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:36:- [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: Seln's knowledge (audit B6): he has inferred that the boy set his figures all season and spent his whole bank at Norhold on purpose (the two slips and the stove; the unmarked file; Jask and the stair job); he was outside the council and does not know a sealed thing exists until M6. The Anchor notice text stays verbatim (BOOK_MAP §8).]
