   120	
   121	He was quiet a moment.
   122	
   123	"It is the only sentence I have left that they still need. I intend to make them do without it."
   124	
   125	Seln said one thing during the refusals and only one, and he said it after the second, without moving from his chair. "You will want to write it down somewhere. Everybody does, the first year. Do not."
   126	
   127	Vastin looked at him for a moment — the two of them the only people in the room who had ever done this — and said, "No. I know what that costs."
   128	
   129	Karis asked the one procedural question, because somebody had to and it was hers. "Will they proceed?"
   130	
   131	"Yes."
   132	
   133	"Then what does the refusal buy?"
