   152	
   153	"No," said Karis, gathering the nine documents back into the folder with hands that were not entirely steady and would have denied it. "He didn't take anything at all. That's the part I'm going to be thinking about."
   154	
   155	Seln checked the courtyard, and then the stair, and then the street, and came back and said the only assessment that mattered, in a tone that made it sound already filed.
   156	
   157	"He came up the front stair. He knocked at an open door. He told us he had told no one, before he was asked." He picked up the folder. "A man arranging a betrayal does none of those things. He was not managing us. In nineteen postings I have met four people who were not managing me, and I did not like any of them either."
